1 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Metta is often translated as loving-kindness, and at its root is something very simple: <strong>friendliness</strong>. </p><p>Not so much politeness, not people-pleasing, and definitely not pretending everything is fine. </p><blockquote><p>A friendly heart is one that learns to wish well, even when life feels difficult, even when another person is difficult, even when we ourselves feel difficult to love.</p></blockquote><p><em>This does not mean we abandon boundaries.</em> </p><p>We can say no, disagree, walk away, or hold someone accountable, and <strong>still choose not to feed hatred and hostility in our own hearts</strong>. </p><p><em>Metta is not weakness.</em> </p><p>It is a quiet strength that helps us soften the sharp edges of resentment without denying what has happened.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"819\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:819,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:151917,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/206785174?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ay26!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F282b0bbe-036a-4cc1-b430-f5c5e5038dbd_1920x1080.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The practice can begin simply. </p><p>Bring to mind someone you care for and offer a few quiet phrases: <em>May you be happy. May you be healthy.</em> </p><p>Then, slowly, extend the same wishes to yourself, to someone neutral, to someone challenging, and eventually to all beings.</p><p>Some days, the words may feel mechanical, and that is okay. </p><p>The heart does not always open dramatically. <strong>Sometimes it softens subtly, almost imperceptibly.</strong></p><div class=\"pullquote\"><p><strong>To practise metta is to remember that beneath our defences, there is still a friendly heart waiting to be uncovered.</strong></p></div><p><span>At Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 11 - 12 July 2026, we practiced extending thoughts of kindness and unconditional goodwill to ourselves and others. We closed the session with a reading from the book </span><a href=\"https://wisdomexperience.org/product/loving-kindness-plain-english/\"><span>Loving Kindness in Plain English</span></a><span> by Bhante Gunaratana. </span></p><h3><strong>Meditation Practice</strong></h3><blockquote><p><em><strong>Tap Play to Practice Together:</strong></em></p></blockquote><div class=\"native-audio-embed\" data-component-name=\"AudioPlaceholder\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;label&quot;:null,&quot;mediaUploadId&quot;:&quot;e5cf1e6d-ec5a-4e65-b105-297adb295e10&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1286.1388,&quot;downloadable&quot;:false,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true}\"></div><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/uncovering-a-friendly-heart?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">This post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/uncovering-a-friendly-heart?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/p/uncovering-a-friendly-heart?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><div><hr></div><h3><strong>The Wholehearted Woman Retreat</strong></h3><p><strong><span>A five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within</span><br><br></strong><span>1-5 October 2026</span><br><span>Siem Reap, Cambodia<br>*</span><em><span>Limited space available</span></em><br><br><span>Led by Erin Lee</span></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><sou