 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Have a chat with Erin and Subba on the retreat program and details.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Arrange a Personal Chat&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://beingme.com.sg/power-and-pause\"><span>Arrange a Personal Chat</span></a></p>",
  "body_text": "Metta is often translated as loving-kindness, and at its root is something very simple: friendliness. \n\nNot so much politeness, not people-pleasing, and definitely not pretending everything is fine. \n\nA friendly heart is one that learns to wish well, even when life feels difficult, even when another person is difficult, even when we ourselves feel difficult to love.\n\nThis does not mean we abandon boundaries. \n\nWe can say no, disagree, walk away, or hold someone accountable, and still choose not to feed hatred and hostility in our own hearts. \n\nMetta is not weakness. \n\nIt is a quiet strength that helps us soften the sharp edges of resentment without denying what has happened.\n\nThe practice can begin simply. \n\nBring to mind someone you care for and offer a few quiet phrases: May you be happy. May you be healthy. \n\nThen, slowly, extend the same wishes to yourself, to someone neutral, to someone challenging, and eventually to all beings.\n\nSome days, the words may feel mechanical, and that is okay. \n\nThe heart does not always open dramatically. Sometimes it softens subtly, almost imperceptibly.\n\nTo practise metta is to remember that beneath our defences, there is still a friendly heart waiting to be uncovered.\n\nAt Take A Pause Live on Insight Timer over 11 - 12 July 2026, we practiced extending thoughts of kindness and unconditional goodwill to ourselves and others. We closed the session with a reading from the book Loving Kindness in Plain English by Bhante Gunaratana. \n\nMeditation Practice\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nThe Wholehearted Woman Retreat\n\nA five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within\n\n1-5 October 2026\nSiem Reap, Cambodia\n*Limited space available\n\nLed by Erin Lee\n\nJoin Erin at Angkor Wat\n\n---\n\nPower & Pause Retreat\n\nA high-touch program supported by structured processes, guided practices, and reflective assignments\n\n8 - 12 October 2026\n\nUbud, Bali\n\nLed by Subba Sattvic and Erin Lee\n\nHave a chat with Erin and Subba on the retreat program and details.\n\nArrange a Personal Chat",
